---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="The STAR Framework" description="Cosmic storytelling principles that transform how you communicate">
  <article class="rabbit-hole">
    <section class="hero-rabbit">
      <a href="/rabbit-holes/" class="back-link">← Rabbit Holes</a>
      <div class="rabbit-tenets">
        <span class="tenet">Story</span>
        <span class="tenet">Insight</span>
        <span class="tenet">Growth</span>
      </div>
      <h1>The STAR Framework</h1>
      <p class="rabbit-tagline">Cosmic storytelling principles that bypass cynicism and open minds through awe</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Core Insight</h2>
      <div class="insight-box">
        <blockquote>
          "We are a way for the cosmos to know itself. We are made of star-stuff."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="quote-attribution">— Carl Sagan, Cosmos (1980)</p>
        <p>
          Carl Sagan transformed complex astrophysics into profound human narrative by doing something counterintuitive: 
          <strong>he took us further out to bring us closer in</strong>. By shifting perspective to the cosmic scale, 
          he made us care more deeply about our home, our species, and our choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the secret that most business storytelling misses: <strong>awe opens minds that logic cannot</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The STAR Framework</h2>
      <p class="framework-intro">
        A proprietary Word And Mouth methodology synthesizing Carl Sagan's cosmic perspective 
        with the Hero's Journey, StoryBrand, and our Storyselling system.
      </p>
      <div class="star-grid">
        <div class="star-card">
          <span class="star-letter">S</span>
          <h3>Shift</h3>
          <p class="star-tagline">Move perspective to reveal the hidden problem</p>
          <p>
            Zoom out far enough to see what's invisible up close. Like viewing Earth from space — 
            the borders disappear, the fragility becomes clear.
          </p>
          <div class="cosmos-quote">
            "We float like a mote of dust in the morning sky"
          </div>
          <p class="application"><strong>Apply:</strong> Before diving into your solution, take stakeholders to an unexpected vantage point.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="star-card">
          <span class="star-letter">T</span>
          <h3>Tension</h3>
          <p class="star-tagline">Articulate the stakes honestly</p>
          <p>
            Don't hide consequences. Authentic tension creates commitment. 
            But pair it with hope — tension without a path forward creates paralysis.
          </p>
          <div class="cosmos-quote">
            "This is a time of great danger. But our species is young and curious and brave."
          </div>
          <p class="application"><strong>Apply:</strong> Name what could be lost — then show why action is possible.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="star-card">
          <span class="star-letter">A</span>
          <h3>Awe</h3>
          <p class="star-tagline">Introduce wonder that bypasses cynicism</p>
          <p>
            Awe is the most magical emotion humans can experience. It suspends judgment, 
            opens receptivity, and creates the conditions for change.
          </p>
          <div class="cosmos-quote">
            "There is a tingling in the spine, a catch in the voice... as if a distant memory of falling from a great height."
          </div>
          <p class="application"><strong>Apply:</strong> Lead with an insight so surprising it creates wonder before argument.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="star-card">
          <span class="star-letter">R</span>
          <h3>Resolution</h3>
          <p class="star-tagline">Show the path forward with the hero at the centre</p>
          <p>
            Every cosmic journey must return home. The exploration was always about 
            understanding ourselves and making better choices.
          </p>
          <div class="cosmos-quote">
            "By exploring other worlds, we safeguard this one."
          </div>
          <p class="application"><strong>Apply:</strong> Make your audience the hero who carries the insight forward.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">The Seven Cosmic Principles</h2>
      <p class="principles-intro">Distilled from analysing Sagan's storytelling across all 13 episodes of Cosmos.</p>
      <div class="principles-grid">
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">1</span>
          <h4>The Cosmic Zoom</h4>
          <p>Start with the familiar, zoom out to the cosmic, return transformed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">2</span>
          <h4>Star-Stuff Identity</h4>
          <p>Connect personal identity to something larger than individual concerns.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">3</span>
          <h4>Awe Before Argument</h4>
          <p>Lead with wonder, not fear or logic. Awe opens minds that facts cannot.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">4</span>
          <h4>The Honest Stakes</h4>
          <p>Don't hide consequences. Authentic tension creates commitment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">5</span>
          <h4>The Dual Path</h4>
          <p>Present both blessing and curse — knowledge can destroy or liberate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">6</span>
          <h4>Deep Time Perspective</h4>
          <p>Use scale to make today's challenges feel both small and urgent.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-card">
          <span class="principle-number">7</span>
          <h4>The Return Home</h4>
          <p>Every journey must return home. Exploration was always about understanding ourselves.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section endorsement-section">
      <div class="endorsement-box">
        <blockquote>
          "Our loyalties are to the species and the planet. We speak for Earth."
        </blockquote>
        <cite>— Carl Sagan, final episode of Cosmos, 1980</cite>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Framework Comparison</h2>
      <p class="comparison-intro">How STAR relates to other storytelling methodologies:</p>
      <div class="comparison-table">
        <div class="comparison-header">
          <span>Framework</span>
          <span>Core Structure</span>
          <span>Best For</span>
          <span>STAR Integration</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-row">
          <span class="framework-name">Hero's Journey</span>
          <span>12-stage transformation arc</span>
          <span>Epic narratives, brand origin stories</span>
          <span>Resolution phase uses hero's return</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-row">
          <span class="framework-name">StoryBrand</span>
          <span>Customer is hero, business is guide</span>
          <span>Marketing messages, website copy</span>
          <span>Shift + Resolution positioning</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-row">
          <span class="framework-name">Pixar Story Spine</span>
          <span>"Once upon a time... Until one day..."</span>
          <span>Quick pitches, founding stories</span>
          <span>Tension phase momentum</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-row">
          <span class="framework-name">Freytag's Pyramid</span>
          <span>5-act dramatic structure</span>
          <span>Presentations, case studies</span>
          <span>Full arc mapping</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comparison-row highlight">
          <span class="framework-name">STAR Framework</span>
          <span>Shift → Tension → Awe → Resolution</span>
          <span><strong>Breaking through cynicism and stuck thinking</strong></span>
          <span>Unique: adds cosmic perspective + awe</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Application by Persona</h2>
      <div class="persona-applications">
        <div class="persona-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Founder CEOs</span>
          <h4>"We're growing but lack clarity"</h4>
          <p><strong>Use SHIFT:</strong> Zoom out from daily operations to market-level perspective. What cosmic-scale problem does your industry actually solve?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="persona-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Marketing Directors</span>
          <h4>"Content doesn't convert"</h4>
          <p><strong>Use AWE:</strong> Lead with a transformative insight, not features. Create wonder before making your ask.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="persona-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Sales Leaders</span>
          <h4>"Pitches don't resonate"</h4>
          <p><strong>Use TENSION:</strong> Articulate what's at stake honestly. Your prospect already knows their problem — acknowledge the real cost.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="persona-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Product Leaders</span>
          <h4>"Users don't understand our value"</h4>
          <p><strong>Use RESOLUTION:</strong> Show the user as the hero completing their journey. Your product is the guide, not the destination.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="persona-card">
          <span class="persona-tag">Strategy Consultants</span>
          <h4>"Need to unlock growth"</h4>
          <p><strong>Use FULL STAR:</strong> Reframe the entire competitive landscape. Take clients to a perspective their competitors haven't considered.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Why Awe Works</h2>
      <div class="science-box">
        <p>
          Research shows that <strong>awe expands our perception of time</strong>, making us more patient and willing to invest in long-term thinking. 
          It also <strong>reduces self-focus</strong>, increasing our sense of connection to others and causes larger than ourselves.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is why climate change messaging often fails: fear contracts thinking, awe expands it. 
          Sagan knew this intuitively — he made us feel small in the cosmos to make us care more about each other.
        </p>
        <p class="key-insight">
          <strong>The counterintuitive truth:</strong> Going "out of this world" concentrates the senses through fixation, surprise, excitement, and awe.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-label">Connected Methodologies</h2>
      <div class="connected-box">
        <h3>STAR + Storyselling</h3>
        <p>
          The STAR framework provides the <em>storytelling principles</em>. 
          <a href="/rabbit-holes/storyselling/">Storyselling</a> provides the <em>business process</em> for implementing them.
        </p>
        <div class="connection-visual">
          <span>STAR (Principles)</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
          <span>Storyselling (Process)</span>
          <span class="arrow">→</span>
          <span>Solution Story (Output)</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Use STAR when you need to <strong>break through</strong> — when logic isn't working, when audiences are cynical, 
          when the challenge requires a fundamentally different perspective.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section cta-section">
      <h2>Ready to shift your perspective?</h2>
      <p>Let's find the cosmic vantage point that makes your story undeniable.</p>
      <a href="mailto:dave@wordandmouth.com?subject=STAR%20Framework" class="cta-button">Start the Conversation</a>
    </section>

    <footer class="article-footer">
      <div class="related-links">
        <h4>Explore Related</h4>
        <a href="/rabbit-holes/storyselling/">Storyselling →</a>
        <a href="/story/">Story Tenet →</a>
        <a href="/insight/">Insight Tenet →</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .rabbit-hole {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-rabbit {
    padding: 10rem 2rem 4rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .rabbit-tenets {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tenet {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .hero-rabbit h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .rabbit-tagline {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .insight-box {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .insight-box blockquote {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .quote-attribution {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .insight-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .insight-box p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .framework-intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .star-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .star-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .star-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);
    position: relative;
  }

  .star-letter {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2px;
    right: 1.5rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .star-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .star-tagline {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .star-card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .cosmos-quote {
    font-style: italic;
    color: #ccc;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .application {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.08);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .principles-intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .principles-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 600px) {
    .principles-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .principle-card {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    position: relative;
  }

  .principle-number {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.75rem;
    right: 1rem;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.3);
  }

  .principle-card h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .principle-card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .endorsement-section {
    border-top: none;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .endorsement-box {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.08) 0%, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.02) 100%);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .endorsement-box blockquote {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .endorsement-box cite {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .comparison-intro {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .comparison-table {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .comparison-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr 1.5fr 1.5fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: #1a1a1a;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .comparison-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr 1.5fr 1.5fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: #111;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #222;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .comparison-row.highlight {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.08);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .framework-name {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .comparison-header,
    .comparison-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    
    .comparison-header span:first-child,
    .comparison-row span:first-child {
      font-size: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .persona-applications {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .persona-card {
    background: #111;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .persona-card:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .persona-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.15);
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .persona-card h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .persona-card p {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .science-box {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .science-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .key-insight {
    background: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.1);
    padding: 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--text) !important;
    margin-bottom: 0 !important;
  }

  .connected-box {
    background: #111;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .connected-box h3 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .connected-box p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .connected-box a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .connection-visual {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .connection-visual span {
    background: #1a1a1a;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
  }

  .arrow {
    background: none !important;
    padding: 0 !important;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .cta-section {
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .cta-section h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .cta-section p {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .article-footer {
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #222;
  }

  .related-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .related-links h4 {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .related-links a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .related-links a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
</style>
